# Jungle announce run of huge summer 2027 UK shows

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from NME Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Jungle have announced a run of massive UK shows for next summer, including a headline slot at Latitude.

The dates come in support of the BRIT-award winning trio dropping their uplifting fifth album ‘Sunshine’ earlier this year – their first since 2023’s ‘Volcano’.

Dates kick off at Bristol’s Queen Square on June 19 and will be one of the first concerts held at the outdoor space since Massive Attack performed a landmark set there in 2003. For over two decades there were no shows held there, until IDLES hosted a huge Block Party there last summer.

Jungle’s performance will follow the same sustainable initiative that IDLES had in place, becoming one of the first large-scale events of their kind in the UK to be powered entirely by batteries and the national grid, without a generator in sight.

### 🎤 Artist Commentary & Key Highlights

The group have also been confirmed as a headliner for Latitude 2027, which returns to Henham Park in Southwold between July 22 and 25. It will be their first slot there since playing on the Second Stage back in 2014, and the other two headliners will be confirmed at a later date.

“We’re super excited to be heading back to Latitude in 2027,” the trio shared. “It’s one of the first festivals we ever played in the UK and to be asked to headline the Obelisk Arena next summer is an honour and we can’t wait.”

On July 25, they’ll perform at Brighton’s On The Beach festival, joining Two Door Cinema Club, Tom Jones, Pete Tong and more as headliners, and on July 31 the trip will play Platt Field in Manchester – their biggest Manchester headline show to date. Next summer will see the first live music held in Platts Field in 15 years, and other huge names confirmed for headline shows include LCD Soundsystem.

Tickets go on sale from 10am on Friday December 4. Visit here for tickets and more information.

### 📊 Background & Industry Impact

Jungle’s UK 2027 shows are:

JUNE19 – Queen Square, Bristol, UK

JULY24 – Latitude Festival, Southwold, UK25 – On The Beach, Brighton, UK31 – Platt Fields, Manchester, UK

With ‘Sunshine’, J Lloyd, Tom McFarland and Lydia Kitto captured their signature blend of soul, disco and electronica, and blended it with more relaxed elements, inspired by the 1970s Brazilian music scene. It was previewed with singles ‘Carry On’ and ‘The Wave‘

Jungle are coming to the end of a huge autumn tour across the US, Europe and the UK, as the dates continue tonight (Wednesday November 25) with the second of two nights at The O2 in London, and wrap up with stops in Manchester and Glasgow on November 27 and 28 respectively.

